<title>FRANCE: SOCCER SHOWCASE-ITALY 3 BRAZIL 3 - RESULT.</title>
<headline>SOCCER SHOWCASE-ITALY 3 BRAZIL 3 - RESULT.</headline>
<dateline>LYON, France 1997-06-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy and Brazil drew 3-3</p>
<p>in their Tournoi de France match on Sunday.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Italy - Alessandro Del Piero 7, 62 pen, Aldair 24 own goal</p>
<p>Brazil - Attilio Lombardo 35 own goal, Ronaldo 71, Romario 84</p>
<p>Halftime: Italy 2 Brazil 1</p>
<p>Attendance: 32,000</p>
<p>Teams:</p>
<p>Brazil- 1-Taffarel; 6-Roberto Carlos, 3-Aldair, 15-Celio</p>
<p>Silva, 2-Cafu, 8-Dunga, 5-Mauro Silva (19-Flavio Conceicao 63),</p>
<p>10-Leonardo, 20-Denilson, 9-Ronaldo, 11-Romario</p>
<p>Italy - 12-Gianluca Pagliuca; 13-Christian Panucci, 5-Fabio</p>
<p>Cannavaro, 6-Alessandro Costacurta, 3-Paolo Maldini (7-Angelo Di</p>
<p>Livio 89), 23-Attilio Lombardo, 10-Demetrio Albertini, 8-Roberto</p>
<p>Di Matteo, 4-Dino Baggio (18-Diego Fuser 46), 19-Christian Vieri</p>
<p>(21-Filippo Inzaghi 59), 20-Alessandro Del Piero</p>
<p>Referee: Serge Mumenthaler, Switzerland</p>
<p>Standings:</p>
<p>		    P     W     D     L    F     A    Pts</p>
<p>    England     2     2     0     0    3     0     6</p>
<p>    Brazil	2     0     2     0    4     4     2</p>
<p>    France	2     0     1     1    1     2     1</p>
<p>    Italy	 2     0     1     1    3     5     1</p>
<p>Previous matches:</p>
<p>    June 3: Lyon:	  France 1 Brazil 1</p>
<p>    June 4: Nantes:	England 2 Italy 0</p>
<p>June 7: Montpellier: France 0 England 1</p>
<p>Remaining matches:</p>
<p>    June 10: Paris:	England v Brazil</p>
<p>    June 11: Paris:	France v Italy</p>
</text>
